hen youâ€™re responsibilities-maxxing, sometimes you need the opposite. A blowout. A huge, transcendent, resetting release. A rave.</p><p>I donâ€™t know what took me so long to get around to it. Misplaced parental guilt? Internalised ageism? Exhaustion? Itâ€™s not as though I didnâ€™t know other gen-Xers who have been regularly getting blissfully â€“ ceremonially, even â€“ lost in house, techno or drumâ€™nâ€™bass, and theyâ€™re not alone. <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/03057356251329229">A 2025 study</a> by the University of Leeds went viral: â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DXmbIDPDbpf/">Women aged 40-65 are turning to raves for real mental health</a>,â€ said one of many Instagram posts and press headlines. â€œ<a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DZbTO7vFcNi/?img_index=1">Why many women over 40 still go to raves</a>,â€ read another. But surely the question should be: why the hell wouldnâ€™t they?</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/20/the-rave-secret-why-middle-aged-women-are-larging-it-and-seeing-big-health-benefits">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;VWXtkRj_TwwqfbKd8FOvN5m99OY0UPkqmTaTqmCgNdcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;kEEpsVVMqEUoDYegXUwlz5ABH7NSac14sGnY2pCUSlQƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;czZAX5UCHhMh1ivbVte1salvZxy7mUtPWt27zvg3Ww8ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0nOQAZ4RBCeZGUnsfkWEbzfhmXeyLdAJaINNjOds_20ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;zrZYc27L5ut6qLVzI9qRE9kRpIoVKWC4OVhD7wlAVXwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9yy2ZDGxXux